{
  "comment": "MyPaint brush file",
  "version": 3,
  "description": "Wet flat",
  "notes": "TOOL, operator `pull` (rapier_op 7). A broad flat brush carrying clean water, used to pull a wash out: transport and dilution in one dab, over a flat footprint whose long edge stays across the hand, so the paint is drawn forward AND thins as it goes -- a graded wash rather than a smear. It never lays the selected colour.\n\nWhat an artist reaches for it to do, and its whole contract: docs/paint-tools.md.\n\nAuthor: Rapier\nLicense: AGPL-3.0-only",
